Z||000000||Monkeyman||01-21-2001||07:26 AM||||Finally finished installing my new stereo in the as-yet-unnamed GT.  Sony CDX-650 CD head unit, Kenwood amp, JBL 5 1/4" separates, and a powered Bazooka tube.  Currently I have the Bazooka tube behind the passenger seat, but that's getting moved to the front of the seat this morning (seat sits up waaaaay too far).  I still need to finish some minor details.  The mids aren't mounted yet, just resting in the stock openings, I'm still working on the faceplate for the tweeters, and the amp is just mounted to the firewall.  Hopefully, the amp rack will be done sometime in the next couple of weeks.<P>I wasted most of a tank of gas last night just driving around listening to the music.  <P>A hotrod Fiero with a cool stereo.  What else does a man need? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||overlord||01-21-2001||09:55 AM||||its weird, ive been into stereo stuff for a while but not nearly as much since i got my fiero. And ever since my cousin heard some thumping, then seeing my fiero come around the corner.....got him into stereo stuff for his car too....Which reminds me....im gonna upgrade my cd headunit sooon......teehee...im gettin all giddy again....||||reg||1
